I’ll look for studies that directly connect neighborhood context, recreational physical activity, and survival among breast cancer survivors, then assess how strong and direct the evidence is.

Tool call: go_search_agent
Tool call input: {'knowledge_bases': ['pubmed_papers'], 'search_rounds_budget': 3, 'search_target': 'Find and summarize peer-reviewed studies investigating whether neighborhood characteristics or neighborhood influence/context modifies recreational physical activity and survival after breast cancer. Focus on breast cancer survivor cohorts, neighborhood socioeconomic status/built environment/social environment, recreational or leisure-time physical activity, all-cause or breast-cancer-specific survival, and whether neighborhood context moderates activity-survival associations. Provide study design, cohort/sample, key effect estimates, and PMID/DOI.'}
